le story details  there's a wide array of analysis and  theory videos for you to enjoy all with  vastly different takes and ideas one  thing that is worth mentioning is that  around this time people started  discovering a lot of parallels between  some of the teaser footage and concept  art included in masterworks particularly  the one where link's arm is either  damaged or mutated or transforming into  all sorts of weapons and tools it was  speculated that whatever was happening  to link's arm could serve as the basis  for all kinds of new powers and  abilities especially since the sheikah  slate is nowhere to be seen in the  coming days from june 11 to 18 onuma  took part in a series of interviews in  which he would answer a few burning  questions and reveal some additional  tidbits of information albeit not much  while talking to ign on the show floor  of e3 he mostly stuck to the subject of  link's awakening which was set to  release in september but he did share a  few things about the sequel because of  the darker tone of the footage and the  fact that it's a direct sequel ign asked  if the game was perhaps inspired by  majira's mask the sequel to ocarina of  time and considered to be one of the  darkest entries in the series to which  anuma responded that the game will not  necessarily be related to or inspired by  majira's mask and that it just so  happens that what they showed in the  teaser was a bit darker this quote  quickly spread around like wildfire and  was used as proof that the game would be  even darker than the n64 classic however  many have since spoken up against this  presumption suggesting that it's a  misinterpretation of anuma's words and i  agree the phrase what we showed you  currently is a little bit darker is  clearly a general statement about the  nature of the teaser itself and not in  reference to majira's mask that isn't to  say that the game won't have its fair  share of darker elements though i mean  the stuff we see here is defin