ut an article by gamesradar  covering the topic does still exist and  that rounds up 2019 at least when it  comes to news about the sequel link's  awakening released on the 20th of  september however no further comments  were made on breathtawa 2 by any of the  staff and so we were left waiting for  the next major update little did we know  that we were about to enter what came to  be known as the great nintendo drought  of 2020  [Music]  as the pandemic took the world by  surprise nintendo news in general would  slow down to an absolute crawl the  second and third quarter were  particularly barren for switch owners  many pointed out that the japanese work  culture isn't exactly well adapted to  working remotely and so it's all but  certain that breathtaking's development  suffered some significant slowdown  during this period and it shows because  for the next 18 months there were no  major updates to the game at all no new  footage no release date no title nothing  on july 6 there was a short-lived  controversy regarding two spanish voice  actors which gave fans a shimmer of hope  that maybe the game was in a much  further state of development than  originally thought and could show up  again soon after all it was reported  that on a local podcast the voice actors  for rivali and zelda said that they were  done working on the spanish dub of the  game in the industry it's common  knowledge that the localization takes  place in the final stages of development  and means that the animations dialogue  and thus the story have all been  finalized however these reports would  later be corrected or retracted  altogether as it became clear that there  was a lot of nuance and context missing  from the language used and knowing what  we know now this was indeed a classic  case of fake news the only official  update we got this year came in  september when hyrule warrior's age of  calamity was unexpectedly announced on  twitter prior to showing the new  warriors title aonuma 